ine suggests a marginal hand, likely a single pair (like an 8, 3, or a newly hit 10) or a low pocket pair. Since the 10 is a high card, if the opponent has a 10, they will likely call a bet. If I check, I miss an opportunity to extract value and give a free card that could potentially counterfeit my hand (e.g., if the board pairs the 3 or 10 on the river).\n\nReason: I have a strong hidden hand (Two Pair) and the opponent has shown passivity. I want to build the pot and extract value from worse hands such as Top Pair (Tens) or Second Pair (Eights) that the opponent might be holding. A bet of 300 (half the current pot of ~600) is a solid value bet that is likely to be called by inferior hands without pushing them out too aggressively.\n\nAnswer: 300'}
