ly fold, meaning I gain no value. Stronger hands (any 10, any 8 with a better kicker, or higher pocket pairs) will call or raise, costing me money. Since the opponent has checked, I have the opportunity to check back and see a free showdown. This avoids losing to a trapped 10 or a better 8 while securing the pot if my hand is still best against their lower range.\n\nReason: My hand strength was reduced by the river pairing the board with a card higher than my pairs (counterfeiting). Betting has negative expected value because worse hands fold and better hands call. Checking is the safest and most profitable play to realize showdown value.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
